## Marketplace: bind Lakebase at install again

Context: On 2026-11-12 Lakebase was dropped from manifest.yaml because the
SDK's AppManifestAppResourceSpec (0.82) has no postgres spec. That was wrong:
the Apps manifest accepts `postgres_spec`, and Ontos, Lakemeter and the
app-templates ship it (PLAN.md Q1). Lakebase is an install-time resource
again; the installer creates a Lakebase project first and picks it in the
install dialog.

Changes:

1. marketplace/manifest.yaml
   Declares the `postgres` resource (postgres_spec, CAN_CONNECT_AND_CREATE).
2. marketplace/app.yaml
   Header comment: Lakebase is bound at install.
3. marketplace/LISTING.md
   "Before installing" (create a Lakebase project), Lakebase in the
   install-time table, three post-install steps.
4. scripts/marketplace/emulate_install.py
   --lakebase-branch is required; validate_branch runs before any CLI call;
   a failing CLI call prints its stderr instead of a traceback.
5. tests/units/scripts/test_marketplace_package.py
   AUTO_INJECTED_RESOURCES = {"postgres"}; replaces the SDK-model test with
   test_manifest_binds_lakebase_at_install.
6. tests/units/scripts/test_marketplace_emulate_install.py
   Resource names match the manifest with Lakebase; a missing branch is rejected.
7. marketplace/README.md, .planning/marketplace-listing/PLAN.md
   Q1 correction; 2026-11-24 dogfood results.

Modified files:
- marketplace/manifest.yaml
- marketplace/app.yaml
- marketplace/LISTING.md
- marketplace/README.md
