## First-run registry setup for Marketplace installs

Context: A Marketplace install has no deploy step and no REGISTRY_CATALOG /
REGISTRY_SCHEMA, so Initialize could not run (PLAN.md Q7). Its service
principal also lacked Can Manage on its own app, which locked every user out
(Q4). The first admin can now open Settings → Registry → Set up the registry
and pick a catalog and schema. Acting as that admin (user scopes `sql` and
`apps`), the app gives its service principal Can Manage on the app, creates
the schema, and grants the service principal its UC privileges. It then runs
Initialize, which stores the location in Lakebase. The `apps` scope also lets
an admin in before any grant. Verified end to end in E2 dogfood on
ontobricks-mp-test-013. A fresh-context review found no security issue; its
findings on retry, race and error classification are fixed.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/RegistrySetupService.py (new)
   The admin-side steps: app Can Manage grant (a warning on failure), then
   CREATE SCHEMA and least-privilege GRANTs over the Statement Execution API.
   It uses the caller's token with auth_type="pat", because the app's own
   client id/secret are also in the env. Not-found names become
   ValidationError, missing privileges become AuthorizationError, and a
   statement that times out is cancelled.
2. src/back/objects/registry/__init__.py
   Re-exports RegistrySetupService.
3. src/back/objects/domain/settings/RegistrySettings.py
   setup_registry_result prepares the schema and pins the location on the
   session, then runs Initialize. It refuses to move an existing registry,
   checks again on a fresh read after preparing, and unpins if Initialize
   fails. initialize_registry_result falls back to the saved Lakebase row when
   neither env nor session pins a location, which fixes "Apply upgrades"
   returning 400 after a redeploy.
4. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   POST /settings/registry/setup is admin-only and passes the forwarded user
   token. A malformed body returns 400.
5. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_registry_configuration.html
   "Set up the registry" form (catalog, schema), hidden until registry.js
   shows it.
6. src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js
   Shows the form only while no location is set, hides the env-var hint in
   that state, updates the not-configured message, and exposes
   window.reloadRegistryConfig.
7. src/front/static/config/js/settings-registry-configuration.js
   Form submit handler, with native validation, showNotification, and the
   results shown in the existing grants panel.
8. marketplace/manifest.yaml, marketplace/app.yaml
   Add the `apps` user scope (Marketplace only; the DAB deploy grants Can
   Manage in app-permissions.sh).
9. marketplace/LISTING.md, marketplace/README.md, docs/deployment.md,
   .planning/marketplace-listing/PLAN.md
   LISTING is down to two post-install steps; the docs gain a "Installing from
   Databricks Marketplace" section; the README and PLAN record the
   2026-11-24 (013) results.
10. tests/units/registry/test_registry_setup.py (new),
    tests/units/front/test_settings_registry_setup_form.py (new),
    tests/units/scripts/test_marketplace_package.py
    Cover the service, setup orchestration (guard, race, unpin), route
    (admin-only, bad body), the Initialize fallback, the form contract, and
    MARKETPLACE_ONLY_SCOPES.

